{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of upward momentum: When sentiment history shows a cluster of high values (1.00) following a price dip, the model's flat or declining forecast fails to capture the subsequent sharp rally (e.g., +10-15 EUR spikes). Apply a positive momentum adjustment to the forecast immediately after sentiment turns strongly positive.",
    "Adjust for excessive mean reversion lag: The model assumes a slow return to a lower mean (approx. 70-72 EUR) even when true prices sustain higher levels (80-90 EUR) for extended periods. Reduce the speed of the mean reversion parameter in the model when sentiment remains elevated for more than 3 consecutive days.",
    "Mitigate overshoot on downside: The model forecasts a gradual decline that is too slow compared to the actual rapid drop seen in late November 2023. When sentiment drops to 0.00 after a peak, accelerate the downward slope of the forecast to match the steeper historical volatility.",
    "Horizon-specific bias correction: The model exhibits a consistent negative bias (under-prediction) in the 10-20 day horizon during bull runs and a positive bias (over-prediction) during bear runs. Apply a dynamic bias correction factor based on the 5-day average sentiment score.",
    "Sentiment-weighted volatility scaling: The model's forecast range is too narrow (low volatility) compared to the true outcome's wide swings. Increase the forecast variance significantly when the standard deviation of the sentiment history exceeds 0.4."
  ]
}
